#Problem APEX 2.2.5

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Applications of differentiation)
## DBsection(Linear approximation and differentials)
## KEYWORDS('function approximation', 'linearization')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## MLT(LinearApprox_GeneralFunction)
## Level(2)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('2.2')
## Problem1('5')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$a  = random(80, 120);
$b  = random(20, 80);
$c  = random(1,  20) * random(-1, 1, 2);
$dx = random(1,  9) * random(-1, 1, 2);
$a1 = $a + $dx;

$ans = Real($b + $c * $dx);

BEGIN_PGML
Given that [` P([$a]) = [$b] `] and [` P'([$a]) = [$c] `], approximate
[`P([$a1])`].

[`P([$a1]) \approx`] [_]{$ans}{10}.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Using the formula, [` f(c + h) \approx f(c) + f'(c)\cdot h `], with the function [`P`],  [`
  P([$a1]) = P([$a] + [$dx]) \approx P([$a]) + P'([$a])\cdot ([$dx]) 
  = [$b] + [$c] \cdot ([$dx]) = [$ans].
`]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
